{"flags":[{"id":"price-breakdown-balance-beam","fault":"breaks the job","why":"Tilt angle encodes the amounts and the SVG is aria-hidden, so the net result is hard to read at a glance and the picture carries the job."},{"id":"price-breakdown-tri-fold-panel","fault":"breaks the job","why":"Panels folded behind the total hide the breakdown, and hinge-by-hinge opening slows reading; the fold is a picture more than a structure."},{"id":"price-breakdown-exchange-pipeline","fault":"vague","why":"The travelling dot and the node states are not specified, and the sent, fee, rate and received math is left open (what is fee-deducted, what is multiplied)."},{"id":"price-breakdown-live-meter","fault":"low buildability","why":"Live updates, rolling digits and a ghost range are rated 3 but need a data feed and a custom digit roller, and the live region rules are loose."}],"rewrites":[{"id":"price-breakdown-balance-beam","element":"price-breakdown","name":"Two sided balance table","how":"Two stacked groups, amount back and deductions, each list their lines with a toggle per line and a group sum, and a thin SVG beam above tilts at most 8 degrees toward the larger sum while a net row beneath prints the exact figure in text.","buildability":3,"rtl":"The amount back group sits on the right and deductions on the left in Arabic, the beam tilt direction follows the heavier side, and figures keep normal digit order.","a11y":"1.1.1 Non-text Content: the beam is decorative with aria-hidden, and the net row and both group sums are real text so nothing depends on the tilt.","pages":["returns","transaction-detail","subscription-management"]},{"id":"price-breakdown-tri-fold-panel","element":"price-breakdown","name":"Stacked fold panels","how":"Items, fees and payment are three stacked panels under an always visible total bar, each panel header is a button that opens or closes its panel with a 200 ms height transition, and a small tilt on the header chevron shows the state.","buildability":4,"rtl":"Panel text and chevrons align to the right in Arabic, the stack stays vertical, and amounts keep normal digit order.","a11y":"4.1.2 Name, Role, Value: each header is a button with aria-expanded and aria-controls, and the total bar stays visible and readable whether panels are open or closed.","pages":["order-confirmation","booking","doctor-booking","transaction-detail"]},{"id":"price-breakdown-exchange-pipeline","element":"price-breakdown","name":"Conversion pipeline steps","how":"An ordered vertical list of four nodes shows sent amount, minus fee, times rate, and received amount, each node a row with a label and figure joined by a 2 px line, and the received node is larger and the rate node shows the rate with its timestamp.","buildability":4,"rtl":"Node labels sit on the right of the line in Arabic, the flow stays top to bottom, and the rate and amounts keep normal digit order.","a11y":"1.3.2 Meaningful Sequence: use an ol so the order sent, fee, rate, received is read in the same sequence as the math, with the operation named in each item text.","pages":["send-money","transfer-confirmation","crypto-trade"]},{"id":"price-breakdown-live-meter","element":"price-breakdown","name":"Live ticking meter","how":"During a ride the base fare, distance and time rows show current amounts that refresh every 10 seconds from polled data, changed digits cross fade for 150 ms, and a text line under the running total shows the estimated range.","buildability":4,"rtl":"Labels align right in Arabic while amounts, distance units and time keep normal digit order.","a11y":"2.2.2 Pause, Stop, Hide: provide a pause updates button that freezes the figures, and announce the running total through a polite live region at most once a minute.","pages":["trip-in-progress","rate-driver"]}]}
