{"flags":[{"id":"divider-pattern-coded-rule","fault":"vague","why":"Does not say how many patterns exist, how the table of contents entry is built, or what the current-section state looks like; also leans on pattern recognition to find place."},{"id":"divider-marquee-band","fault":"breaks the job","why":"A scrolling band of footer links is a moving target that is hard to click and read, and the footer divider should not carry primary navigation."},{"id":"divider-unread-marker","fault":"breaks the job","why":"Fading a marker on a timer can hide it from slow readers; the rewrite removes the timer."}],"rewrites":[{"id":"divider-pattern-coded-rule","element":"divider","name":"Numbered dash rule","how":"Each top-level section opens with a 2px dashed rule whose dash length steps through a set of four CSS custom property patterns, with the section number and title printed as text above the rule, and the table of contents repeats the same number and a small swatch of the pattern, with the current entry marked by a thicker rule as the user scrolls, using an IntersectionObserver.","buildability":4,"rtl":"The dashes and the section number start from the right edge in Arabic, and the table of contents swatch sits at the start of each entry.","a11y":"1.3.3 Sensory Characteristics: the section number and title stay as visible text, and the current entry also gets aria-current=\"true\" so the pattern is never the only cue.","pages":["legal-page","help-center","faq-page","settings"]},{"id":"divider-marquee-band","element":"divider","name":"Footer section tab strip","how":"The band above the site footer is a static row of footer section names, each a link to its footer column, that wraps onto several lines on narrow screens, with the link under the pointer or focus getting a 2px underline that slides in over 150ms.","buildability":5,"rtl":"The row reads from the right in Arabic, and the names follow the logical inline order of the footer columns.","a11y":"2.4.4 Link Purpose (In Context): each link shows its section name as visible text and has a visible focus ring, and nothing moves on its own so 2.2.2 does not apply.","pages":["footer","news-home","event-page"]},{"id":"divider-unread-marker","element":"divider","name":"Persistent unread marker","how":"A colored rule with the label \"new\" is inserted above the first unread message or comment and stays in place until the user scrolls it above the viewport or leaves the thread, and then it is removed on the next visit.","buildability":4,"rtl":"The label sits at the end edge, so it moves to the left in Arabic and reads \"جديد\".","a11y":"2.2.1 Timing Adjustable: no timer hides the marker, and it is exposed as role=\"separator\" with an aria-label such as \"new messages\" so screen reader users can find it.","pages":["support-chat","comments","news-home"]}]}
