{"flags":[{"id":"hero-breathing-circle","fault":"breaks the job","why":"Looping animation is only paused by a button, and the In/Out label states are unclear for screen readers."},{"id":"hero-redaction-bars","fault":"breaks the job","why":"Bars hide the headline, so users without scroll or with motion off may never see the statement, and the reveal depends on viewport entry."},{"id":"hero-field-aware-panel","fault":"vague","why":"Does not say which scenes exist, how they map to fields, or what happens on blur."},{"id":"hero-turntable-dish","fault":"breaks the job","why":"Endless rotation and a spin on each swap risk making the dish name and order button hard to use and read."}],"rewrites":[{"id":"hero-breathing-circle","element":"hero","name":"Paced breathing circle","how":"A 160px circle holds the session title and a Start button, and before start it stays still at 70 percent; after Start it scales to 100 percent over 4 seconds and back over 4 seconds, with a text label switching between In and Out at each turn, and a visible Pause button that freezes the circle and the label.","buildability":5,"rtl":"The labels use Arabic noun forms such as شهيق and زفير while the circle, scale and timing are identical in both directions.","a11y":"2.2.2 Pause, Stop, Hide: the Pause button is a native button placed right after the circle, the circle stays still under prefers-reduced-motion with the text label alone showing the phase, and the phase label sits in a polite live region.","pages":["meditation-session","first-run","splash-screen"]},{"id":"hero-redaction-bars","element":"hero","name":"Lifting redaction bars","how":"The full headline is real text, with key words wrapped in spans that carry a solid bar pseudo-element; the bars slide off one by one every 400ms once the hero is visible, and a Reveal all button removes every bar at once.","buildability":5,"rtl":"Bars slide off toward the start edge of each word and the reveal order follows right to left reading order in Arabic.","a11y":"1.3.2 Meaningful Sequence: the words stay in the DOM in reading order from the start so screen readers get the full statement, and under prefers-reduced-motion the bars are removed with no animation.","pages":["manifesto-page","campaign-page","launch-page"]},{"id":"hero-field-aware-panel","element":"hero","name":"Field aware side panel","how":"A brand panel beside the form holds three scenes (email, password, and a default), each an illustration with one line of text; when a field gets focus its scene crossfades in over 300ms and when focus leaves the form the default scene returns.","buildability":4,"rtl":"The panel sits on the left of the form in Arabic and any directional illustration uses a mirrored version.","a11y":"3.2.1 On Focus: focus and form layout never change when the panel swaps, and the panel is outside the form and aria-hidden since it only repeats nonessential content.","pages":["login","sign-up","forgot-password","bank-onboarding","identity-verification"]},{"id":"hero-turntable-dish","element":"hero","name":"Turntable dish photo","how":"A round cut out food photo sits on a plate shape that turns once, 360 degrees over 8 seconds, on load and then stays still; Previous and Next buttons swap the dish with a quick 400ms spin, and the dish name and order button below update in place.","buildability":4,"rtl":"The Previous and Next buttons swap sides and the dish name aligns right, while the spin stays clockwise.","a11y":"2.2.2 Pause, Stop, Hide: the single turn ends by itself, under prefers-reduced-motion the plate does not rotate and dishes swap with a fade, and the dish name sits in a polite live region.","pages":["restaurant-menu","restaurant-site","product-detail","grocery-home"]}]}
