{"flags":[{"id":"sidebar-tear-off","fault":"low buildability","why":"Rated 2: free-floating panels with docking and drag need heavy custom work."},{"id":"sidebar-rotary-dial","fault":"breaks the job","why":"A rotating dial for primary navigation is slow and hard to use, and the rotated label ring is hard to read, especially in Arabic."},{"id":"sidebar-book-spines","fault":"breaks the job","why":"Rotated titles on narrow spines are hard to read and truncate, which hurts a sidebar's navigation job."}],"rewrites":[{"id":"sidebar-tear-off","element":"sidebar","name":"Pop out section panel","how":"Each section header has a pop-out button that moves the section into a fixed-position floating panel (320px wide, with a title bar and a dock button), leaving a dashed placeholder row in the sidebar; the dock button returns it to its slot, and the open or docked state is saved per section.","buildability":3,"rtl":"Floating panels open at the left of the sidebar when the sidebar is on the right, and the title bar buttons swap sides.","a11y":"2.1.1 Keyboard: pop-out and dock are real buttons, the floating panel is a labelled region, and focus moves to its title on pop out and back to the placeholder button on dock.","pages":["document-editor","analytics-dashboard","kanban-board","invoice-builder"]},{"id":"sidebar-rotary-dial","element":"sidebar","name":"Section switch wheel","how":"A vertical stack of 3 to 6 section tabs sits at the top of the sidebar with a round selector knob that slides to the chosen tab and clicks into place, while the list below swaps to that section's items with a 150ms crossfade.","buildability":4,"rtl":"The tab labels align right, the knob sits on the right edge of the stack, and the list below mirrors.","a11y":"4.1.2 Name, Role, Value: build it as a radio group or tablist with arrow key selection and aria-selected so no pointer rotation is needed.","pages":["analytics-dashboard","gov-services-dashboard","investment-portfolio","settings"]},{"id":"sidebar-book-spines","element":"sidebar","name":"Expanding course shelf","how":"Courses are listed as 40px horizontal rows with a colored edge strip, and selecting one expands it in place to a card with a cover, title and progress bar while the others stay collapsed, one open at a time.","buildability":4,"rtl":"The edge strip moves to the right side of each row and the cover sits on the right in the expanded card.","a11y":"4.1.2 Name, Role, Value: each row is a button with aria-expanded, and the expanded card shows progress as text such as \"40 percent complete\".","pages":["course-catalog","reading-mode","course-lesson","profile"]}]}
