{"flags":[{"id":"list-row-countdown-ring","fault":"breaks the job","why":"Updating the ring every minute and draining it live is hard to read as a time, and a ring that only shows for the next row hides the other rows' times unless each row also has text."},{"id":"list-row-hold-to-confirm","fault":"breaks the job","why":"A hold on a destructive row cannot be used by many users, and Enter held down fires repeated key events, so the keyboard path is fragile."},{"id":"list-row-proportional-height","fault":"breaks the job","why":"Row height set by value share makes small rows tiny and large rows huge, so the list is hard to scan, and the 24 px floor in the a11y line conflicts with the 44 px floor in the how."},{"id":"list-row-fare-staircase","fault":"breaks the job","why":"Indenting rows by price rank shifts the text edges and makes scanning and comparing harder, and the indent can overflow at narrow widths."},{"id":"list-row-tally-marks","fault":"low buildability","why":"Hand drawn tally strokes that animate in fives need custom SVG paths and handling for big counts, and it is rated 3 with unclear behavior past about 20."}],"rewrites":[{"id":"list-row-countdown-ring","element":"list-row","name":"Countdown ring lead","how":"Each row starts with a 32 px SVG ring and a text line such as in 1 h 20 min, where only the next upcoming row has a ring whose stroke-dashoffset shows the share of time left, past rows show a dimmed check and future rows show an empty ring, and the text updates once per minute.","buildability":3,"rtl":"The ring moves to the right side in Arabic and keeps draining clockwise, while times and the minute count keep their digit order.","a11y":"1.4.1 Use of Color: every row shows its remaining or past time as text and state words such as next, done or later, so the ring is never the only cue.","pages":["prayer-times","calendar","appointment-booking","trip-in-progress","habit-tracker"]},{"id":"list-row-hold-to-confirm","element":"list-row","name":"Hold to confirm","how":"A destructive row has a Delete button where a plain click opens a confirm dialog, and a press and hold of 1.5 seconds fills the row background from the leading edge and runs the action when full, or drains back to empty if released early, and the Space key held does the same using keydown and keyup with repeat ignored.","buildability":4,"rtl":"The fill grows from right to left in Arabic so it starts at the leading edge.","a11y":"2.5.1 Pointer Gestures and 2.1.1 Keyboard: the plain click that opens a confirm dialog is the full alternative, so the hold is optional and the same action works by keyboard.","pages":["account-deletion","subscription-management","api-keys","team-members","settings"]},{"id":"list-row-proportional-height","element":"list-row","name":"Share bar rows","how":"Each row keeps a fixed 56 px height and holds a label, an amount and a percentage in text, with a bar under the label whose width equals that row's share of the total, and the bars animate width over 300 ms when values change.","buildability":5,"rtl":"Labels and amounts swap sides in Arabic and the bar grows from the right edge.","a11y":"1.4.1 Use of Color: the percentage is shown as text in each row so the bar length is never the only cue, and the row stays at least 44 px tall for 2.5.8 Target Size.","pages":["budget-overview","analytics-dashboard","investment-portfolio","transactions","year-in-review"]},{"id":"list-row-fare-staircase","element":"list-row","name":"Price gap labels","how":"Option rows are sorted by price with no indent, the cheapest carries a Lowest price tag, every other row shows a plus amount label for its gap to the cheapest, and the selected row gets a thicker border and a lift shadow.","buildability":5,"rtl":"Gap labels and the tag move to the left end in Arabic, and prices keep their digit order.","a11y":"1.4.1 Use of Color: the gap is written as text such as plus 40 riyals and the selected row shows a check mark, so neither depends on color or position.","pages":["flight-search","ride-booking","plan-picker","insurance-quote","hotel-detail"]},{"id":"list-row-tally-marks","element":"list-row","name":"Tally mark count","how":"Each row draws its count as SVG tally groups of four vertical strokes crossed by a fifth diagonal, logging one more animates the next stroke with stroke-dashoffset over 200 ms, and counts above 20 collapse to the marks for the remainder plus a numeric count.","buildability":4,"rtl":"The tally group moves to the left end in Arabic and new strokes are added from the right, with the numeric count unchanged.","a11y":"1.1.1 Non-text Content: show the count as text next to the marks and give the SVG a role of img with an aria-label giving the total.","pages":["habit-tracker","activity-summary","workout-player","year-in-review"]}]}
