{"flags":[{"id":"loading-self-sketching-skeleton","fault":"vague","why":"Does not state timing, per-block sequence or the swap to content, and the stroke direction in RTL is not buildable as written."},{"id":"loading-wave-letter-word","fault":"breaks the job","why":"The how says letters move in sequence, but the rtl line says the word animates as a whole, so they contradict and Arabic joins break."},{"id":"loading-poppable-dots","fault":"breaks the job","why":"Interactive toys in the loading area pull focus from the status and add many tab stops, which hurts the loading message's job."}],"rewrites":[{"id":"loading-self-sketching-skeleton","element":"loading","name":"Outline then fill skeleton","how":"Each skeleton block is an SVG rect with a 1px outline whose stroke-dashoffset animates from full length to 0 over 600ms, staggered 80ms per block from top to bottom, then the rect fills with a flat tint over 200ms, and when data arrives the real content cross-fades in over 200ms and the SVG is removed.","buildability":4,"rtl":"Mirror the SVG with scaleX(-1) in Arabic so strokes start at the top right, and anchor block widths to the right edge.","a11y":"2.3.3 Animation from Interactions: under prefers-reduced-motion show the filled blocks at once with no stroke draw, and set aria-busy on the container until content lands.","pages":["loading-state","chat-thread","support-chat","notifications","search-results"]},{"id":"loading-wave-letter-word","element":"loading","name":"Wave letter word","how":"For Latin text, each letter of the loading message sits in its own inline-block span that rises 4px and returns on a 1.2s loop with a 60ms stagger per letter, and for Arabic text the whole line is one element that rises and falls together so joins stay intact, and on completion the motion stops and the full message rests in place.","buildability":4,"rtl":"Arabic uses a single whole-line bob with no letter splitting, and Latin letter stagger runs left to right only in Latin text.","a11y":"4.1.2 Name, Role, Value: keep split letter spans aria-hidden and give the container one readable label with role status, and stop the motion under prefers-reduced-motion.","pages":["loading-state","search-results","splash-screen","chat-thread"]},{"id":"loading-poppable-dots","element":"loading","name":"Optional pop dots","how":"Below the progress status text, a loose 5 by 4 grid of 32px soft dots sits in an area marked as optional play, tapping a dot scales it to 0 over 150ms and it regrows after 2s, and a Skip play button removes the grid and the dots are not in the tab order until the user activates a Play button.","buildability":4,"rtl":"The grid is symmetric and does not mirror, and the status text and the Play and Skip buttons align right.","a11y":"2.5.8 Target Size (Minimum): each dot is at least 32 by 32 pixels with 8px spacing, the dots stay out of the tab order until Play is pressed, and the status text comes first in reading order with role status.","pages":["loading-state","splash-screen","search-results","support-chat"]}]}
