{"flags":[{"id":"cta-balance-beam-plans","fault":"breaks the job","why":"Tilting beam with hover-only price drop makes the plan CTA unclear, and no single clear action or keyboard-selectable state is defined."},{"id":"cta-plan-card-stack","fault":"breaks the job","why":"Plans hidden behind a fanned stack hide prices from comparison, and the Start button changes meaning with the top card."},{"id":"cta-marquee-band-button","fault":"breaks the job","why":"A scrolling band as the only CTA makes the label hard to read and hit, and it fails the pause requirement unless the label is also static."}],"rewrites":[{"id":"cta-balance-beam-plans","element":"cta","name":"Beam plan picker","how":"Two or three plan buttons sit in a row under a thin SVG beam; selecting a plan (click, tap, or arrow keys in a radio group) tilts the beam 4 degrees toward it and lowers that plan's price tag by 8 pixels, the recommended plan is preselected, and one Continue button below always acts on the selected plan and names it.","buildability":3,"rtl":"Plan order runs right to left in Arabic, and the beam tilts toward whichever plan is selected, not in a fixed direction.","a11y":"4.1.2 Name, Role, Value: plans are a radio group with the selected state exposed to assistive tech and shown by a thick border and a Selected label, and the beam stays level under reduced motion.","pages":["pricing-page","plan-comparison","plan-picker","upgrade-modal"]},{"id":"cta-plan-card-stack","element":"cta","name":"Plan card deck","how":"Plans are shown as a fanned stack where each card's edge shows its name and price at all times, selecting a card slides it 16 pixels forward and expands its feature list, and one Start button below the stack always reads Start with the selected plan name.","buildability":3,"rtl":"The fan opens toward the left in Arabic, and prices and billing periods keep left to right digits.","a11y":"1.3.2 Meaningful Sequence: the DOM is a radio group in plain plan order so keyboard and screen reader users pick from a simple list, and the slide is replaced by an instant change under reduced motion.","pages":["paywall","plan-picker","upgrade-modal","subscription-management"]},{"id":"cta-marquee-band-button","element":"cta","name":"Marquee band link","how":"A full width band repeats a large call to action phrase in a slow sideways scroll, the band is one link with a single static accessible name, hovering speeds it up, focus stops it, and a visible Pause button next to it freezes it with the first phrase fully readable.","buildability":4,"rtl":"The text scrolls from left to right in Arabic so new words enter from the reading start, and the Pause button sits at the leading edge.","a11y":"2.2.2 Pause, Stop, Hide: a visible Pause control is provided, the scroll is off under prefers-reduced-motion, and the link text is one static name rather than the repeated copies.","pages":["landing-page","campaign-page","launch-page","newsletter-signup","footer"]}]}
